el to the  physical world but he's now found a way  through dorothy's power of making  imaginary creatures come to life  as witnessed throughout the season the  candle maker can grant wishes but these  wishes come at great expense which is  why nyle says she must never make a wish  in the comics the candlemaker allows  three wishes kind of like a genie  and it just so happens she uses her  final wish to bring back  joshua clay one of the murder doom  patrol members add that to the list of  reasons we may see him again  upon using her final wish the  candlemaker gets its freedom into the  physical world  which is what dorothy is wanting to stop  now i don't think the candlemaker is  going to kill dorothy  he needs dorothy in order to get into  the physical world her power  is what makes it possible for him to  live but i do want to talk about the  candlemaker's last  line where he tells dorothy it's time  for her to meet her fate does he know  what she'll become  what she'll be responsible for will he  even try to sway her against niles and  the doom patrol  after all it was niles who kept her  hidden away on dany street for decades  almost like a prisoner now i also see  the show introducing a time travel  element and there are some clues that  hint towards this  time has played a huge role this season  nice wants to slow down dorothy growing  up and wears a longevity talisman  something he trades to willoughby  kipling in order to return the doom  patrol members to their natural size  there's also an interesting episode  where rita and cliff have to take on a  dr  time who controls a rare time bending  element called  continuinium not to mention how the show  utilizes countless flashbacks but it's  the fact cliff won't be able to make his  daughter clara's wedding that leads me  to believe time travel might just happen  i mean it would be the perfect ending if  a time travel element were introduced  and cliff and the doom patrol are both  able to save the day  and 